      "title": "KDSP: Prevent some bogus expert info warnings",
      "message": "KDSP: Prevent some bogus expert info warnings\n\nThe server version and hostname fields are 32 octet\nfixed length fields that contain null terminated strings,\nand the bytes after the null terminators can have anything.\nChange them to FT_STRINGZTRUNC, so that they don't warn\nabout garbage octets.\n\nThe NULL command needs to have no-op handling instead of\nthe default in the command switch statement to avoid a\nwarning about an unknown command type.\n\nTested with the sample capture on the SampleCaptures wiki page.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
